# Per-finding allowlist for the `secrets` job in .github/workflows/validate.yml.
# Auto-discovered from the repo root, so validate.yml passes no -i flag.
#
# This file is the ONLY approved way to clear a betterleaks finding. Do not delete
# .betterleaks.toml, and do not widen or drop its sk-ant- rule: stock rules anchor
# sk-ant-api03- and sk-ant-admin01- to an exact 93-char body, so removing that rule
# silently restores a green scan on the Claude Code OAuth pair (sk-ant-oat01-,
# sk-ant-ort01-) it exists to catch. An entry here suppresses one line; every other
# finding still fails the job.
#
# The job runs `betterleaks git`, so a fingerprint is commit:file:rule-id:startline
# -- four fields, NOT the three a `betterleaks dir` report prints. Copy it from
# `betterleaks git . -c .betterleaks.toml --report-format json --report-path -`.
#
# One entry per line, each preceded by a comment saying why it is not a real leak.
# No entries yet: full history currently scans clean.
